{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacking configurations, the researchers analyzed Raman and photoluminescence data to identify stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses. Atomic-resolution microscopy confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. The study developed a framework explaining SHG intensity and polarization orientation across configurations, demonstrating TT-MoS2 as a tunable nonlinear optical platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual twisted interfaces in trilayer MoS2 create stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses",
    "Atomic-resolution techniques confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "A framework linking dual interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization orientation"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown twisted trilayer MoS2 configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanism for tuning nonlinear optical responses in van der Waals materials through multi-interface twisted stacking, advancing the design of tunable photonic devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses residual tumor persistence after high-frequency irreversible electroporation (H-FIRE) for prostate cancer. By identifying DNA damage repair as the key mechanism for reversible cell survival, researchers engineered a piezoelectric nanomaterial (BOIS) that leverages H-FIRE-induced membrane permeability. BOIS, activated by ultrasound, generates an electric field and reactive oxygen species to convert residual cells from reversible to irreversible damage, significantly enhancing tumor eradication without additional external energy input.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BOIS nanomaterial exploits H-FIRE-induced membrane permeability for targeted delivery",
    "Ultrasound activation of BOIS produces dual mechanisms: electric field-mediated membrane damage and oxidative stress",
    "This approach converts residual tumor cells from reversible to irreversible damage, improving eradication efficacy"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a self-reinforcing therapeutic loop where focal ablation serves as a delivery mechanism for nanomaterials, enabling enhanced tumor eradication through intrinsic dual-action mechanisms without additional external energy input."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated metabolic heterogeneity in small cell lung cancer (SCLC) by analyzing transcriptomic and metabolomic data across neuroendocrine (NE) and non-NE cellular states. It identified a universal cysteine dependency and demonstrated that NE cells with low ASCL1 undergo ferroptosis upon cysteine depletion, while ASCL1high cells undergo apoptosis and resist ferroptosis due to GCH1-mediated BH4/BH2 upregulation. Combined cysteine depletion and BH4/BH2 inhibition reduced tumor growth in xenografts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SCLC cells exhibit universal cysteine dependency across neuroendocrine and non-neuroendocrine states",
    "ASCL1low NE cells undergo ferroptosis when cysteine is depleted, whereas ASCL1high cells undergo apoptosis and resist ferroptosis",
    "ASCL1 directly activates GCH1 transcription, increasing BH4/BH2 antioxidants to confer ferroptosis resistance"
  ],
  "study_type": "Integrated transcriptomic and metabolomic analyses",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish metabolic state as a determinant of cell death susceptibility in SCLC, offering a metabolic target for overcoming therapy resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of achieving low threshold voltage (Vth) and high performance in n-type organic electrochemical transistors (OECTs). Using a stepwise cyanation strategy on quinoxaline-based polymers, researchers developed QxCN-CNTVT, which exhibits a deep LUMO level (-4.23 eV), low Vth (0.13 V), high µC* (168.89 F cm-1 V-1 s-1), and stability. The material enables efficient amplification of electrooculogram (EOG) and electrocardiogram (ECG) signals and integrated logic gates.",
  "key_findings": [
    "QxCN-CNTVT achieves a low threshold voltage of 0.13 V",
    "The polymer demonstrates a high µC* value of 168.89 F cm-1 V-1 s-1",
    "QxCN-CNTVT enables efficient EOG and ECG signal amplification and logic gate implementation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Synthetic molecular design",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a molecular strategy to simultaneously optimize low threshold voltage and high performance in n-type OECTs, advancing low-power bioelectronic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates hydrogel adhesives designed for hemorrhage treatment and wound closure with phase-transition-regulated wet adhesion and removal. The researchers developed a hydrogel (PANA) exhibiting strong wet adhesion (61.2 ± 9 kPa) at body temperature and weak adhesion (5.3 ± 2.2 kPa) at 20 °C for easy detachment. The hydrogel achieves rapid hemostasis in rabbit injuries and allows gentle removal via phase separation when exposed to cold saline. Combined with cold plasma, it inhibits bacterial growth to accelerate healing. The findings address the challenge of maintaining effective adhesion while enabling safe removal without secondary injury.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PANA hydrogel demonstrates strong wet adhesion (61.2 ± 9 kPa) at body temperature for effective hemorrhage control",
    "The hydrogel exhibits weak adhesion (5.3 ± 2.2 kPa) at 20 °C, enabling gentle removal without secondary damage",
    "Cold plasma activation with PANA inhibits bacterial proliferation, accelerating infected wound healing"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo testing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a clinically relevant solution for hemorrhage management by balancing robust wet adhesion with on-demand removal, reducing the risk of secondary injury during surgical procedures."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates industrialization's impact on the human metaorganism by analyzing gut microbiome, immunoglobulin A, host genotyping, diet, lifestyle, and fecal biomarkers across globally diverse populations. It demonstrates industrialization correlates with homogenized microbial compositions, reduced diversity, lower community stability, elevated gut stress markers, increased IgA secretion, and altered IgA-bacteria interactions. Microbiome disease predictors from industrialized groups fail in less industrialized cohorts, indicating limited cross-population applicability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Industrialization correlates with homogenized microbial compositions",
    "Industrialization is linked to reduced microbial diversity and lower community stability",
    "Microbiome disease predictors trained on industrialized populations are uninformative in less industrialized cohorts"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings reveal coordinated restructuring of the microbial ecosystem and host physiology under industrialization, emphasizing the need for globally representative data to improve translational microbiome applications across diverse human populations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the research redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with reduced expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalability for practical battery applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C",
    "The design reduces electrode thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 2 Ah NCM811 pouch cells with 80% capacity retention after 1200 cycles"
  ],
  "study_type": "Material design and synthesis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing critical mechanical and electrochemical instability challenges in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used CRISPR mutagenesis to map functional elements within the MYC gene locus at base-pair resolution. It found 67% of essential base pairs are noncoding, with an ultraconserved RNA element in the 3' UTR critical for MYC protein localization. Targeting this element with ASOs selectively kills cancer cells and inhibits tumor growth, highlighting noncoding sequences as key functional regulators and identifying a druggable target.",
  "key_findings": [
    "67% of functionally essential base pairs in the MYC locus are noncoding",
    "An ultraconserved noncoding RNA element in the MYC 3' UTR promotes perinuclear mRNA localization and nuclear protein localization",
    "Steric-blocking ASOs targeting this RNA element selectively eliminate MYC-dependent cancer cells and inhibit tumor organoid growth"
  ],
  "study_type": "CRISPR tiling mutagenesis",
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that noncoding sequences are major carriers of functional genetic information and identifies a druggable RNA element that disrupts MYC-driven cancer mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a static-dynamic synergistic interfacial remediation strategy to enhance aqueous zinc metal batteries. By forming a dual-phase In/Sb composite layer on Zn and using In3+ in the electrolyte for dynamic regulation, the approach suppresses dendrite growth and parasitic reactions. The system achieves stable cycling for over 6000 hours in symmetric cells and demonstrates high energy density in practical pouch cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dual-phase In/Sb composite layer on Zn suppresses dendrite growth and parasitic reactions",
    "In3+ in the electrolyte dynamically regulates interfacial stability during cycling",
    "The system enables stable cycling for over 6000 hours in symmetric cells and high energy density in practical pouch cells"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro electrochemical testing with symmetric and pouch cells",
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy provides a practical interfacial design for durable, high-capacity aqueous zinc batteries, addressing key limitations in long-term cycling stability and energy density."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used bioorthogonal proteomics to investigate blood-brain barrier protein transport in healthy and Alzheimer's disease models. It found the healthy BBB samples 191 plasma proteins and permits 92 into the brain, enriched for carrier and metabolic functions. These proteins target specific cell types via receptor hand-offs, with APOA1 engaging astrocytic ABCA1 to support synapse integrity. Early Alzheimer's models show reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, while hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescues deficits in these models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The healthy blood-brain barrier samples 191 plasma proteins and permits 92 into the brain parenchyma",
    "APOA1 crosses the BBB via SR-B1 and engages astrocytic ABCA1 to support synapse integrity",
    "Early-stage Alzheimer's models exhibit reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, with hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescuing deficits"
  ],
  "study_type": "Bioorthogonal proteomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work redefines the blood-brain barrier as a selective interface that recruits neuroprotective circulatory proteins to maintain brain health, highlighting a critical pathway for Alzheimer's disease pathogenesis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of achieving uniform zinc deposition in aqueous batteries by introducing micropore high-entropy single-atoms carbon nanoparticles (CuNiMnCoIr/CNs) as an electrolyte additive. The additive suppresses interfacial Zn2+ concentration polarization, enhances Zn2+ transport, and promotes layer-by-layer deposition. It achieves a high Zn2+ transference number of 0.89 and enables stable cycling for over 4000 hours at 5 mA cm-2.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Micropore high-entropy single-atoms carbon nanoparticles (CuNiMnCoIr/CNs) suppress interfacial Zn2+ concentration polarization",
    "The additive enhances Zn2+ transport and desolvation kinetics, reducing migration energy barriers",
    "Achieves a Zn2+ transference number of 0.89 and enables stable cycling beyond 4000 hours at 5 mA cm-2"
  ],
  "study_type": "Electrolyte additive",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides atomic-level insights into mitigating interfacial supersaturation in aqueous zinc batteries, advancing fundamental understanding of metal deposition mechanisms for next-generation energy storage systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how aging impacts distinct cell types, brain regions, and sexes in primates using a single-nucleus atlas of macaque brain tissue. By integrating recent data, it identifies context-dependent aging programs, sex-biased transcriptional aging, and molecular connections to Alzheimer's disease, revealing heterogeneity in aging effects across the primate brain.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Context-dependent aging programs vary across brain regions",
    "Sex-biased transcriptional aging patterns are observed",
    "Molecular links between aging and Alzheimer's disease are identified"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-nucleus atlas of macaque brain tissue",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide a comprehensive map of aging effects in the primate brain, highlighting cellular and regional heterogeneity that informs understanding of neurodegenerative disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study compares mechanoactive biomaterials that convert external triggers into controlled mechanical inputs for cell-matrix mechanotransduction. It evaluates hydrogels, light-responsive matrices, thermoresponsive systems, and optothermal actuators based on their mechanical response, cellular input, spatial/temporal control, reversibility, cytocompatibility, and translational feasibility. The findings highlight how these platforms modulate integrin signaling, cytoskeletal dynamics, YAP/TA, and TGF-β pathways to inform design principles for predictive in vitro models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mechanoactive biomaterials convert external triggers into mechanical inputs with defined timing, magnitude, and spatial localization",
    "These platforms modulate integrin-focal adhesion signaling, cytoskeletal dynamics, YAP/TAZ activity, and TGF-β activation",
    "Design principles for selecting reversible or persistent actuation and matching mechanical parameters to tissue mechanics are established"
  ],
  "study_type": "Comparative analysis of mechanoactive biomaterial platforms",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances the field by establishing design principles for mechanoactive biomaterials that precisely control mechanical inputs to cells, enabling more accurate in vitro models of cell-matrix mechanotransduction."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines how liquid biopsies and artificial intelligence converge to improve cancer detection and monitoring through blood-based biomarkers. It addresses challenges like signal sparsity and heterogeneity, highlighting AI's role in extracting tumor-derived information from noisy data. The study emphasizes multimodal AI models' potential to enhance sensitivity while acknowledging clinical and infrastructural barriers.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Liquid biopsies capture tumor signals via circulating biomolecules in blood",
    "Multimodal AI models improve sensitivity for tumor detection in noisy data",
    "Clinical and infrastructural barriers limit current implementation of AI-enhanced liquid biusing"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances understanding of AI-integrated liquid biopsy approaches for more precise cancer monitoring, demonstrating how multimodal models can overcome signal heterogeneity challenges in blood-based diagnostics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a plasmonic coacervate platform for detecting polystyrene micro/nanoplastics (MNPs) in water. The platform uses liquid-liquid phase separation to form microdroplets that spontaneously capture and enrich negatively charged PS MNPs with high efficiency. The co-encapsulated silver nanoparticles create SERS hotspots, achieving an enhancement factor of 2.72 × 10^9 and detecting PS at concentrations as low as 1 ng/mL. The method demonstrates strong performance in real-world water samples and food-contact materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "99.4% enrichment rate for nanoscale PS MNPs",
    "91.1% enrichment rate for microscale PS MNPs",
    "Minimum detectable concentration of 1 ng/mL for nano- and 10 ng/mL for micro-scale PS"
  ],
  "study_type": "Plasmonic coacervate platform with liquid-liquid phase separation",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a sensitive, rapid method for detecting micro/nanoplastics in environmental and food-contact materials using spontaneous sequestration and plasmonic amplification."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated single-cell multiomic maps of adult human brain regions, integrating transcriptional and histone modification data. It identified cell-type-specific regulatory mechanisms, developmental epigenetic memory patterns, and improved interpretation of neurological variants. These findings establish a framework for understanding brain cell identity, evolution, and pathology.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cell-type-specific regulatory landscapes in adult human brain regions",
    "Developmental epigenetic memory patterns",
    "Enhanced interpretation of neurological variants through multiomic profiling"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell multiomic atlases",
  "scientific_significance": "The work provides a comprehensive framework for deciphering human brain cell identity, evolutionary trajectories, and pathological mechanisms through integrated epigenomic and transcriptomic profiling."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines interface-mediated architectural engineering strategies for silicon anodes in solid-state batteries to address volume expansion, interfacial instability, and poor conductivity. It categorizes approaches based on silicon-solid electrolyte coupling, emphasizing design principles, multiscale construction, and mechanisms to improve compatibility, transport, stress management, and reaction control. The study identifies scalable pathways for practical silicon-based solid-state batteries with enhanced energy density and safety.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Categorization of silicon-solid electrolyte architectures by coupling mode",
    "Design principles and multiscale construction methodologies for interface stability",
    "Scalable manufacturing protocols for practical silicon anodes in solid:state batteries"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes a systematic framework for optimizing silicon anodes in solid-state batteries by integrating interfacial engineering with transport and mechanical properties, advancing the field toward practical high-energy-density systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates conserved striatal mechanisms in autism spectrum disorder (ASD) using a cross-species approach. Yuan et al. identified alterations in specific striatal neurons and astrocytes, revealing potential cellular and molecular pathways underlying striatal dysfunction in ASD. The findings suggest novel targets for understanding ASD pathophysiology.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Alterations in specific striatal neurons",
    "Alterations in striatal astrocytes",
    "Cross-species identification of striatal changes relevant to ASD"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides evidence for conserved striatal cellular and molecular mechanisms across species that contribute to ASD pathophysiology, advancing understanding of striatal dysfunction in neurodevelopmental disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines biomass DNA's potential as a sustainable material platform, contrasting synthetic DNA with naturally derived resources. It outlines applications in hydrogels, bioplastics, organogels, and energy storage systems, emphasizing carbon neutrality and multifunctional uses. The study identifies biomass DNA as a scalable resource for next-generation biopolymer applications through a 'Biomass DNA Tree' framework.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Biomass DNA enables recyclable bioplastics supporting carbon neutrality",
    "Biomas DNA organogels and fibers facilitate energy storage in supercapacitors and batteries",
    "Biomass DNA applications span catalysis, soft robotics, OLEDs, and medical devices"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes biomass DNA as a scalable, sustainable platform for multifunctional advanced materials, advancing biopolymer engineering toward carbon-neutral applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used single-nucleus RNA sequencing to analyze 3.9 million nuclei from 178 adult human brains, focusing on striatal and prefrontal cortical variation. It found common patterns of astrocyte, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cell abundance across gray matter regions. Age-related gene expression shifts varied by cell type, with donor age predictable from RNA patterns (median error 6.6 years). Genetic variants influenced nearly 10,000 genes, predominantly cell-type specific and distinguishing striatal from cortical neurons.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Common astrocyte, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cell abundance patterns across gray matter regions",
    "Age-related gene expression changes varied by cell type, with donor age predictable from RNA patterns (median error 6.6 years)",
    "Genetic variants associated with nearly 10,000 genes, mostly cell-type specific and distinguishing striatal from cortical neurons"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-nucleus RNA sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive atlas of human brain cellular and gene expression variation, providing a foundation for understanding inter-individual differences and their implications for neurological disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines nanomedicine approaches to cancer metabolic therapy (CMT), addressing challenges like poor drug targetability and short circulation time of conventional therapies. It analyzes reprogrammed cancer metabolism and nanomaterial strategies targeting glucose, lipids, amino acids, nucleotides, and carboxylic acids. The study highlights design principles for precise metabolic modulation and identifies key barriers to clinical translation of CMT.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nanomedicines overcome limitations of conventional cancer metabolic therapies through improved targetability and circulation time",
    "The review details metabolic reprogramming in cancer cells and tumor microenvironment crosstalk",
    "Nanomaterial strategies target multiple metabolic pathways including glucose, lipids, amino acids, nucleotides, and carboxylic acids"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes nanomedicine as a critical platform for advancing cancer metabolic therapy, providing design principles to precisely modulate tumor metabolism and address translational barriers for next-generation cancer treatments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated multimodal single-cell epigenomic and 3: D genome maps of human basal ganglia across eight subregions. It integrated DNA methylation and chromatin conformation data from over 200,000 nuclei, identifying cell-type-specific differentially methylated regions linked to disease heritability. The research characterized distinct neuronal subtypes, including POU6F2+ spiny projection neurons and STR FS PTHLH-PVALB GABA neurons, with implications for Parkinson's disease mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of millions of cell-type-specific differentially methylated regions enriched for distinct transcription factor motifs",
    "Characterization of POU6F2+ spiny projection neurons with concordant multi-modal signatures",
    "Revealing region-specific methylation and contact gradients near Parkinson's disease risk variants"
  ],
  "study_type": "Multimodal single-cell epigenomic and 3D genome atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides the first comprehensive cell-type-resolved epigenomic and 3D genome maps of human basal ganglia, advancing understanding of regulatory mechanisms underlying motor control and neurological disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This review addresses resistance fluctuations in stretchable electronics under mechanical deformation by identifying two design paradigms: top-down geometric decoupling (e.g., 3D buckling) and bottom-up network reconstruction (e.g., liquid metals). It evaluates fabrication challenges and system integration, emphasizing strain-insensitive conductors' role in bioelectronics, wireless communications, and thermal safety while highlighting future manufacturing and stability goals.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Structurally strain-insensitive conductors use 3D buckling or kirigami to dissipate strain",
    "Intrinsically strain-insensitive conductors maintain percolation via liquid metals or nanofillers",
    "Strain-insensitive conductors enable motion artifact elimination in bioelectronics and thermal safety in high-power applications"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes foundational design principles for strain-insensitive conductors, advancing the field of stretchable electronics by resolving critical mechanical stability challenges for real-world applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a single-cell multi-omic atlas of histone modifications and transcriptomes from eight human basal ganglia regions to map cell-type-specific regulatory landscapes. It identified homeobox transcription factors as key molecular descriptors for neuronal identities and revealed regional heterogeneity in epigenomic and transcriptional programs. The atlas also interpreted noncoding risk variants for neuropsychiatric disorders and enabled predictive modeling of gene regulatory activities.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of homeobox transcription factors as distinctive molecular descriptors for neuronal cell identities in the basal ganglia",
    "Regional heterogeneity in epigenomic and transcription:al programs across basal ganglia regions",
    "Application of the atlas to interpret noncoding risk variants associated with neuropsychiatric disorders"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell multi-omic atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive regulatory framework for understanding human basal ganglia organization, evolution, and disease mechanisms through integrated epigenomic and transcriptomic profiling."
}
